    <name><text>S3 Q1 — Build a JSON-RPC request</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<div style="background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:5px solid #f7931a;border-radius:8px;padding:18px 22px;margin-bottom:16px;">
<p style="color:#9a3412;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 8px;">S3 Q1 — JSON-RPC request</p>
<p style="color:#1e293b;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;margin:0;">A Bitcoin Core RPC request is a JSON object with fields jsonrpc, id, method and params.</p>
</div>
<p style="font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;">Write <strong><code>rpc_request(method, params, id=1)</code></strong> that returns the JSON string for the request, using <code>json.dumps(obj, sort_keys=True)</code> so keys appear in alphabetical order. Use <code>jsonrpc</code> = <code>"1.0"</code>.</p>
<div style="background:#fdf4ff;border-left:5px solid #9333ea;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 18px;margin:12px 0;">
